\title{Adversarial review of the machine's default switch set, of \code{\verb~|k2~}, and of the candidate default (reviewer S3)}
\taxon{Report}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{machine}
\tag{reference-engine}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/soundness-default-set.md}
\meta{moved}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{2026-11-24, 21:06Z - 22:50Z. Two passes. \strong{Pass 1} (sections 0 - 9): \code{\verb~|rlvm-machine~} as published at 20:28Z (jar \code{\verb~|15cb3777e598~}; my private copy \code{\verb~|work/s3/tree~} packages to the same hash), through the JVM launcher of \code{\verb~|work/s3/dist~} (the published jars of the shared distribution of 21:02Z: machine \code{\verb~|15cb3777e598~}, reference \code{\verb~|ca1f9bd918bb~}), \code{\verb~|-Xmx4g~}, one worker. \strong{Pass 2} (section 10, after the owner's decision "practical", OWNER-NOTES note 13): the CANDIDATE default - the default set + \code{\verb~|eager~} + the proof-comparison shortcuts \code{\verb~|skipargs~} and \code{\verb~|congruence~} - on machine jar \code{\verb~|df36be3c8cc9~} (E1's publications of 21:26Z typed bindings, 21:57Z \code{\verb~|eager~}, 22:12Z; my copy \code{\verb~|work/s3/tree2~} packages to the same hash; distribution \code{\verb~|work/s3/dist-cand~}), attacked for a FALSE accept only. No production file was changed; everything of this review is under \code{\verb~|work/s3/~}. Ground truth everywhere: the official checker (\code{\verb~|leanchecker --from-export~}, Lean v4.36.0, inside Docker: \code{\verb~|work/s3/official.sh~}), never the reference engine.}

\p{Switches reviewed: \code{\verb~|same~}, \code{\verb~|pchk~}, \code{\verb~|bodies~}, \code{\verb~|match~}, \code{\verb~|joint~}, \code{\verb~|lazycases~}, \code{\verb~|directrules~}, \code{\verb~|lazyeval~}, \code{\verb~|code~}, \code{\verb~|casetrees~} (the ten that entered \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~} at the wave-6 integration without an adversarial review) and \code{\verb~|k2~} (off). \code{\verb~|warm~} is in the default set and is touched by two findings; \code{\verb~|expect~}, the binder / let / application rules and eager reduction are E1's.}

\p{Words used below. \strong{Kind T}: the machine accepts a statement that is derivable in Lean's type theory and that the official checker rejects only through its own incompleteness, non-transitivity or cache order (evidence: the official checker accepts the same statement in another order, or with the missing step written out). \strong{Kind F}: the accepted statement is not derivable. A machine cell \code{\verb~|M/P~} is the verdict of the PRIMARY machine engine under the switch set (from \code{\verb~|engine.primary.machine.*~}) and the exit status of the pipeline.}

\subtree{
\title{0. Verdict}

\p{\strong{No kind F finding, in the default set and in the candidate (section 10).} Six findings of kind T (certificates in section 3): one in v0 and therefore in every switch set (S3-F1), one in the REFERENCE engine (S3-F2, the default pipeline), one in \code{\verb~|warm~} (S3-F3), and three that are specific to a switch: \code{\verb~|lazyeval~} (S3-F4), \code{\verb~|pchk~} (S3-F5), \code{\verb~|k2~} (S3-F6, with its default thresholds). One finding that is no wrong verdict: \code{\verb~|code~} declines valid units with an internal fault (S3-F7). Under the owner's policy of 22:25Z (kind T tolerated and documented, kind F absolute) the kind T findings are the documented divergences of the default configuration, not blockers. They have one root that none of the gates could see (section 2): \strong{the official \code{\verb~|is_def_eq~} is not a function of its two arguments, not even in plain mode} - the cache \code{\verb~|m_whnf_core~} is read by the cheap \code{\verb~|whnf_core~} calls and written only by the full ones - so every memo of the machine that answers a comparison, a checked type or a cheap CORE is exact only if it mirrors the official per-declaration, term-keyed caches, and none of them does.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Switch}\th{What it assumes}\th{Own difference from the official verdict (beyond v0)}\th{Verdict}}
\tr{\td{(v0, for comparison)}\td{the pair table POS, the tabled CHECKED types and the full-CORE memos are what the official \code{\verb~|m_success~}, \code{\verb~|m_infer_type[0]~}, \code{\verb~|m_whnf_core~} hold}\td{wrong ACCEPT and wrong REJECT, kind T: S3-F1 (9 rows marked \code{\verb~|cache~})}\td{not exact}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|same~}}\td{two values that read back to ONE expression are convertible for the official procedure}\td{none found (0 rows differ from v0)}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded; inherits S3-F1}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|pchk~}}\td{"a closed term without level parameter that passed check mode once passes it in every later declaration"}\td{\strong{wrong ACCEPT, kind T: S3-F5} (4 rows; v0 rejects them)}\td{\strong{not exact}: \code{\verb~|s3-pchk-def-reused-bad~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|bodies~}}\td{the value of a beta body does not depend on having a tabling record; \code{\verb~|(fun .. x .. => x.i) .. a ..~} is \code{\verb~|MKPROJ(a, i)~}}\td{none found}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|match~}}\td{an argument type that equals the domain pattern under the telescope, up to equivalent levels, is convertible with the built domain}\td{none found}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|joint~}}\td{leading binders of type and value with the SAME domain term can be opened once}\td{none found}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lazycases~}}\td{no state of the official lazy-delta loop lies between the unfolding of a \code{\verb~|casesOn~}-shaped definition and the reduct of its recursor}\td{none found}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded (shape CASESON only; a MATCHER tree in the lazy step is NOT exact: row \code{\verb~|s3-lazycases-matcher-over-regular-cases-ok~}, seeded fault 10)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|directrules~}}\td{the rule's right-hand side has the plain form (verified on the term): one APPLY of the minor is the same reduct}\td{none found}\td{exact relative to v0 as coded}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lazyeval~}}\td{"order-only": a one-sided unfolding against a weak-head normal side may run as one WHNF}\td{\strong{wrong ACCEPT, kind T: S3-F4} (v0 rejects)}\td{\strong{not exact}: \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-caseson-lazy-bad~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|code~}, \code{\verb~|casetrees~}}\td{a compiled body / case tree computes the reduct of DELTA + rule + beta}\td{no wrong verdict found; they change which full-CORE memos exist - in my rows always TOWARDS the official verdict (two v0 wrong accepts become rejects of the primary machine); \strong{S3-F7: \code{\verb~|code~} declines valid units (internal fault)}}\td{no difference of their own found; not provably exact (see 4.9); S3-F7 costs a decline}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|warm~} (not on my list)}\td{everything a session keeps is declaration-independent}\td{wrong ACCEPT and wrong REJECT, kind T: S3-F3}\td{not exact}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|k2~} (off)}\td{"the leaf is a reduct of \code{\verb~|c x̄~} by official steps, and reduction commutes with substitution"}\td{\strong{wrong ACCEPT with the default thresholds, kind T, and a wrong REJECT: S3-F6}; with test thresholds also the memo class of S3-F1}\td{\strong{not exact; must stay off} (section 7)}}
}

\p{What follows from it for the default set: under the strict reading of owner note 11 (the official verdict on every input) v0 itself is not a candidate, with or without the ten switches; under the reading "official verdict on real inputs, never a kind F accept" I found nothing against the ten switches - the two that add kind T accepts of their own are \code{\verb~|pchk~} and \code{\verb~|lazyeval~}, and \code{\verb~|warm~} adds its own as well.}

\p{One thing of the PIPELINE, not of a switch: with \code{\verb~|-X engine=machine~} a rejection of the warm machine is re-checked by the strict machine (v0) first and an ACCEPT there is final (E1 saw it for E1-F3). Rows \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-caseson-bad~} and \code{\verb~|s3-wc-inner-matcher-bad~}: the default set REJECTS (the case tree leaves the right memo), v0 accepts, exit status 0. A wrong accept of v0 is a wrong accept of the pipeline whatever the switch set does.}
}

\subtree{
\title{1. Method and tools (all kept under \code{\verb~|work/s3/~})}

\table{
\tr{\th{What}\th{Where}}
